UPDATE companies SET description='Consolidated Telcom, based in Dickinson, North Dakota, traces its roots to January 2, 1961, when the Bowman-Slope Rural Telephone Mutual Aid Corporation and the Dunn Telephone Mutual Aid Corporation merged to form the Consolidated Telephone Cooperative. The cooperative is owned by its members—customers who use its services—and operates as a not-for-profit entity serving southwestern North Dakota.

The cooperative delivers voice, video, and data services across 19 rural communities and the Dickinson area, operating a 100% fiber-to-the-home network in its cooperative exchanges and a hybrid fiber-coax system in Dickinson. Its wholly owned subsidiaries provide competitive local exchange (CLEC) service, internet access, and cable television. Consolidated has invested millions of dollars in network infrastructure since its founding.

Customers include residential subscribers in communities such as Amidon, Dodge, Dunn Center, and Bowman; businesses in Dickinson, Belfield, and Gladstone; and institutions like Dickinson State University, which was the cooperative’s first CLEC customer. The cooperative was originally formed by farmers, ranchers, and local residents who banded together to obtain telephone service that commercial providers deemed unprofitable to offer.

The member-owned structure means a locally elected board of directors governs operations, and revenues above operating expenses are returned to members as capital credits based on usage. Consolidated’s motto, “Reach the World from Here,” reflects its mission to bring urban-level telecommunications to rural areas at comparable cost, driven by a commitment to honesty, integrity, and community service rather than profit.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fiber-to-the-home deployment", "Competitive local exchange (CLEC) services", "Internet service provision", "Cable television distribution", "Voice/telephone service", "Business telecommunications solutions", "Security camera installation and monitoring", "Cybersecurity services"], "industries": ["Residential telecommunications", "Business telecommunications", "Agriculture", "Education", "Rural communities"], "materials": ["Fiber optic cable", "Coaxial cable"], "equipment": ["ONT (Optical Network Terminal)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% fiber-to-the-home network across 19 cooperative communities", "Member-owned cooperative returning capital credits based on usage", "Locally elected board of directors governing operations", "Wholly owned subsidiaries extending service to competitive markets", "Focus on affordable rural telecommunications without profit motive"], "facts_used": ["Founded January 2, 1961 as Consolidated Telephone Cooperative -> /about", "Headquarters in Dickinson, North Dakota -> db", "Member-owned cooperative structure -> /about", "100% fiber-to-the-home in 19 cooperative communities -> /about", "Wholly owned subsidiaries for CLEC, internet, and cable TV -> /about", "Services: Internet, TV, Phone, Business Services, Camera Solutions, Cybersecurity -> /", "Board of directors elected by membership -> /about", "Capital credits returned to members -> /about", "Motto: Reach the World from Here -> /about", "First CLEC customer: Dickinson State University -> /about", "Acquired CATV system in 2000 -> /about", "Invested millions in infrastructure -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Consolidated is the premier provider of telecommunication services in Southwestern North Dakota since 1961.", "founded_year": "1961", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='consolidated-telcom' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Container and Packaging operates from Boise, Idaho, as a wholesale supplier of bottles, jars, and packaging supplies. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or founders.

The company stocks containers in glass, plastic (PET, HDPE, PP), metal, and post-consumer resin (PCR), and offers closures such as pumps, sprayers, and droppers. Beyond distribution, it provides in-house decoration services including screen printing, hot foil stamping, and shrink sleeves, as well as custom boxes, packaging design, label printing, warehousing, logistics, and sourcing through a worldwide network of manufacturing partners. Customers range from small businesses ordering a few hundred units to larger brands requiring pallet quantities.

Container and Packaging serves industries including food storage, chemical and industrial, pharmaceutical, essential oils, art supply, pet care, nutrition and supplement, food and beverage, and personal care. Customer stories highlight brands such as Lone Star Bee Co. (honey), Amallow Skincare & Beauty (tallow creams), and Brwnsgr Skincare (sensitive-skin products), illustrating a focus on small-to-mid-sized consumer-goods companies.

The company emphasizes human-driven service: dedicated account representatives proactively manage accounts, offer multiple shipping options, provide samples, and resolve issues quickly. Its website encourages customers to call for personalized sourcing help rather than relying solely on search, positioning accessible expertise as a key differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen Printing", "Hot Foil Stamping", "Shrink Sleeves", "Custom Boxes", "Packaging Design", "Labels & Printing", "Warehousing & Logistics", "Sourcing"], "industries": ["Food Storage", "Chemical & Industrial", "Pharmaceutical", "Essential Oils", "Art Supply", "Pet Care", "Nutrition & Supplement", "Food & Beverage", "Personal Care"], "materials": ["PET", "HDPE", "PP", "Glass", "Metal", "PCR (Post-Consumer Resin)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dedicated account representatives who proactively manage customer needs", "Human phone support for product sourcing and problem resolution", "In-house decoration: screen printing, hot foil stamping, shrink sleeves", "Warehousing, logistics, and custom packaging design services", "Worldwide network of manufacturing partners for custom sourcing"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Boise, Idaho -> db", "Product categories: glass, plastic (PET, HDPE, PP), metal, PCR containers, closures -> /", "Decoration services: screen printing, hot foil stamping, shrink sleeves -> /", "Additional services: custom boxes, packaging design, labels & printing, warehousing & logistics, sourcing -> /", "Industries served: Food Storage, Chemical & Industrial, Pharmaceutical, Essential Oils, Art Supply, Pet Care, Nutrition & Supplement, Food & Beverage, Personal Care -> /", "Customer examples: Lone Star Bee Co., Amallow Skincare & Beauty, Brwnsgr Skincare -> /", "Differentiators: dedicated account reps, human phone support, samples, multiple shipping options -> /", "Worldwide network of manufacturing partners -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "Wholesale Bottles, Jars & Packaging Supplies; Worldwide Network of Manufacturing Partners", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='container-and-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Contempora Fabrics Inc. was founded in 1972 by Lacy C. Nance in Lumberton, North Carolina. Originally a contract knitter producing fine-gauge interlock and single-knit fabrics, the company transitioned to an employee stock ownership plan (ESOP) in 1984 and became 100% employee-owned by 1988. Today it operates as a fully employee-owned circular knit manufacturer.

The company runs 175 circular knitting machines in a 150,000-square-foot facility on 29 acres, with a production capacity of 2 million pounds of fabric per month. It offers both coarse and fine-gauge knits, supplying greige goods and finished fabrics. Its lint-controlled, humidity-defined manufacturing environment allows simultaneous processing of all fiber types. An in-house research and development team provides fabric analysis and works with customers on the latest fiber and technology trends.

Contempora serves brands, retailers, and manufacturers across performance and activewear, athletic and team apparel, fashion and formal wear, casual and career wear, intimate apparel and shapewear, and swimwear and beachwear. A noted client is Boombah, which credited the company with helping its transition to CAFTA-compliant fabrics. The staff also manages weekly container shipments to Central America under USMCA and CAFTA-DR requirements.

The employee-owned structure is cited as a driver of quality and timely delivery. The company emphasizes competitive pricing, short lead times, and sustainability initiatives including energy-efficient lighting, upgraded HVAC, and recycling of cardboard, yarn scrap, plastic, and paper byproducts.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Circular knitting (coarse and fine gauge)", "Greige goods production", "Finished fabric production", "Fabric analysis", "Research and development", "Contract knitting", "Commission knitting", "Lint-controlled, humidity-defined manufacturing"], "industries": ["Performance & Activewear", "Athletic & Team Apparel", "Fashion & Formal Wear", "Casual & Career Wear", "Intimate Apparel & Shapewear", "Swimwear & Beachwear"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "2 million pounds per month capacity", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% employee-owned (ESOP) structure", "Lint-controlled, humidity-defined manufacturing process", "In-house R&D team for fabric analysis and fiber technology", "USMCA and CAFTA-DR shipping expertise with weekly Central America containers", "Sustainability program: energy-efficient lighting, HVAC upgrades, byproduct recycling"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 by Lacy C. Nance -> /about-us", "Employee-owned (ESOP) since 1984, 100% by 1988 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Lumberton, NC -> db, /, /about-us", "175 machines, 150,000 sq ft on 29 acres -> /about-us", "Capacity 2 million pounds per month -> db, /, /about-us", "Coarse and fine gauge circular knits -> /about-us", "Greige goods and finished fabric sales -> /, /services", "Fabric analysis and R&D -> /, /about-us, /services", "Industries served list -> /, /about-us", "Client Boombah (Jackie) testimonial -> /, /about-us", "USMCA & CAFTA-DR shipping expertise -> /", "Sustainability practices (lighting, HVAC, recycling) -> /", "Lint-controlled, humidity-defined manufacturing -> /about-us", "Short lead times and competitive pricing -> /, /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, Contempora Fabrics is an established manufacturer of all type of circular knits.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["USMCA compliant", "CAFTA-DR compliant", "Weekly container shipments to Central America"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='contempora-fabrics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Continental Manufacturing Chemist (CMC) was founded in 1959 in Madrid, Iowa. The company expanded to a new facility in Huxley, Iowa, in 2018, growing its team to over 150 employees from across Central Iowa.

CMC operates as a contract manufacturer specializing in liquid and paste formulations for personal care and animal care markets. Its capabilities span custom formulation development, reverse engineering, and in-house testing through an R&D team, along with blending and batching in nine tanks ranging from 120 to 3,000 gallons. The facility handles filling from 0.25 ounce to one gallon, including tub, jar, and squeeze-tube lines, plus labeling, cartoning, and manual kitting. Production runs scale from low minimum orders of 10,000 units up to large-volume orders.

The company serves brands in personal care, animal care, baby care, body care, hair care, oral care, and cleaning categories. Customers range from start-ups seeking affordable small-batch production to established OEM and OTC brands. Specific products manufactured include kennel cleaners, wound sprays, flea and tick liquids, shampoos, conditioners, toothpastes, lotions, creams, ointments, body washes, mouthwashes, whitening gels, disinfectants, and hand sanitizers.

CMC differentiates itself with over 60 years of industry experience, turnkey project management from concept to packaging, and a quality system that is FDA registered, MoCRA compliant, and GMP certified. Its location along the Interstate 35 corridor near Iowa State University supports collaboration and rapid response to market demands.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA registered','MoCRA compliant','GMP certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom formulation development", "Reverse engineering", "Product optimization", "In-house testing", "Small-batch production (MOQ \u226410,000 units)", "Large-scale production", "Blending and batching (120\u20133,000 gallon tanks)", "High-shear mixing", "De-aeration", "Filling (0.25 oz \u2013 1 gallon)", "Tub and jar filling", "Squeeze tube filling", "Labeling (front/back, wrap, shrink sleeve)", "Cartoning", "Manual kitting and assembly", "Turnkey project management", "Regulatory support (FDA, MoCRA)", "Stability studies", "Raw material sourcing", "Package development"], "industries": ["Personal care", "Animal care", "Baby care", "Body care", "Hair care", "Oral care", "Cleaning"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["9 batch tanks (120 to 3,000 gallons)", "Lightening agitation", "Shear agitation", "Side sweep agitation", "De-aerator", "Filling lines (0.25 oz to 1 gallon)", "Tub and jar filling equipment", "Squeeze tube filling equipment", "Labeling equipment (front/back, wrap, custom shrink)", "Cartoning equipment", "Manual kitting and assembly lines"], "volume": "MOQ 10,000 units; scalable to large-scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 60 years of contract manufacturing experience", "Low minimum order quantities of 10,000 units or less", "FDA registered, MoCRA compliant, GMP certified", "In-house R&D with custom formulation and reverse engineering", "Turnkey services from formulation to packaging"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1959 in Madrid, Iowa -> /about-us", "Expanded to Huxley, Iowa in 2018; team over 150 employees -> /about-us", "Contract manufacturer specializing in personal care and animal care products -> /", "Capabilities: formulation, flexible manufacturing, turnkey solutions, quality assurance, blending & batching, filling/labeling/assembly -> / and /capabilities", "Low MOQ 10,000 units or less; large-scale production runs -> /capabilities", "9 batch tanks 120\u20133,000 gallons; agitation methods (lightening, shear, side sweep); de-aerator -> /capabilities", "Filling range 0.25 oz to 1 gallon; tub/jar, squeeze tube, labeling, cartoning, manual kitting -> /capabilities", "FDA registered, MoCRA compliant, GMP certified -> /capabilities", "Industries: personal care, animal care, baby care, body care, hair care, oral care, cleaning -> /capabilities and /", "R&D: custom formulations, reverse engineering, product optimization, in-house testing -> /capabilities", "Turnkey services: formula optimization, stability studies, raw material sourcing, package development, regulatory support -> /capabilities", "Location along I-35 near Iowa State University -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a trusted contract manufacturing partner specializing in premium personal care and animal care products.", "founded_year": "1959", "employee_count": "over 150", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "10,000 units", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='continental-manufacturing-chemist' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cope Plastics Inc operates a branch in Fargo, North Dakota, located four miles from Hector International Airport The facility is supported by the company''s headquarters in Alton, Illinois, which houses what the firm describes as the largest collection of CNC plastic fabrication equipment in the Midwest. No founding year or ownership details are disclosed in the available materials.

The Fargo location provides custom plastic fabrication using CNC saws, routers, and drills, producing custom parts, prototypes, and cut-to-size components from engineering plastics. The branch maintains over 7,000 square feet of warehouse space stocked with sheets, rods, and tubes in materials such as HDPE, UHMW, nylon, polycarbonate, and polyurethane, alongside graphic-grade materials like ACM and acrylic. Weekly stocked items include conduit duct spacers, ground protection mats, outrigger pads, and urethane patches.

The company serves industries including fluid handling, food and beverage, construction, mining operations, material handling, and safety and security. Documented applications include solid-lubricant-filled nylon parts for bulk distribution conveyors, food-processing components that eliminate external lubrication, high-temperature polymer parts for kitchen equipment, bearing-grade and oil-filled nylon boom pads for cranes, nylon sheaves for forklifts, and components for mining equipment.

Cope Plastics emphasizes its USA-made fabrication and a streamlined manufacturing process as differentiators from pure distribution companies, citing a commitment to quality and innovation in both materials and manufacturing. The headquarters'' extensive CNC capacity is presented as a core advantage for precision and volume.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC sawing", "CNC routing", "CNC drilling", "Custom plastic fabrication", "Prototyping", "Cut-to-size machining", "Plastic sheet/rod/tube distribution", "Material stocking and inventory management", "Local pickup", "Local delivery (qualifying orders)"], "industries": ["Fluid Handling", "Food & Beverage", "Construction", "Mining Operations", "Material Handling", "Safety & Security", "Medical Device Manufacturing"], "materials": ["ACM", "Acrylic", "Foam PVC", "Fluted Polypropylene", "Flexible Tubing", "HDPE", "HDPE Cutting Board", "Nylon", "Polycarbonate", "Polyurethane", "UHMW", "Solid lubricant filled Nylon", "Oil filled nylon", "Bearing grade nylon", "High-temperature polymer"], "equipment": ["CNC saws", "CNC routers", "CNC drills"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Headquarters in Alton, IL houses the largest collection of CNC plastic fabrication equipment in the Midwest", "USA-made custom plastic parts, prototypes, and cut-to-size components", "Over 7,000 sq ft warehouse in Fargo with comprehensive inventory of engineering plastics", "Local delivery available on qualifying orders", "Streamlined manufacturing process for efficient production and exceptional quality"], "facts_used": ["Fargo branch location 4 miles from Hector International Airport -> page: /", "Headquarters in Alton, IL with largest CNC plastic fabrication equipment collection in Midwest -> page: /", "CNC equipment: saws, routers, drills -> page: /", "Over 7,000 sq ft warehouse space in Fargo -> page: /", "Stocked materials: ACM, Acrylic, Foam PVC, Fluted Polypropylene, Flexible Tubing, HDPE, HDPE Cutting Board, Nylon, Polycarbonate, Polyurethane, UHMW -> page: /", "Weekly stocked products: conduit duct spacers, ground protection mats, outrigger pads, urethane patches -> page: /", "Industries served: Fluid Handling, Food & Beverage, Construction, Mining Operations, Material Handling, Safety & Security -> page: /", "Example applications: solid-lubricant-filled nylon for conveyors, food-processing parts, high-temp polymer for kitchen equipment, bearing-grade/oil-filled nylon boom pads for cranes, nylon sheaves for forklifts, mining equipment parts -> page: /", "USA-made fabrication differentiator -> page: /", "Streamlined manufacturing process for efficient production and exceptional quality -> page: /", "Local delivery on qualifying orders -> page: /", "Services: Saw, Router, Drill, Local Pickup -> page: /", "Contact email  -> page: /", "Company name Cope Plastics Inc -> db", "Branch city Fargo, state North Dakota -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "our fabrication services team delivers high-quality, USA-made parts\u2014distinguishing us from other plastic distribution companies", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cope-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Copper Star Home Medical Supplies operates from Phoenix, Arizona, where it has served the local community for over 22 years. The company runs what it describes as the largest medical supply showroom in the state from a location on East Bell Road near Highway 51, with additional stores in Tempe, Mesa, and Surprise.

The business functions as a durable medical equipment (DME) retailer, offering a broad range of products for sale or short‑term and long‑term rental. Inventory includes power lift chairs, home hospital beds, manual and power wheelchairs, mobility scooters, walkers and rollators, CPAP and BiPAP machines, portable and stationary oxygen concentrators, knee scooters, patient lifts, bath and shower safety equipment, compression garments, orthopedic bracing, and aids to daily living. Every item in the showroom is fully assembled and available for hands‑on trial before purchase or rental. The company accepts FSA and HSA payments and works with major insurance providers including Medicare, Aetna, Blue Cross Blue Shield of Arizona, and several regional health plans.

Customers include patients recovering from surgery, individuals managing chronic respiratory, cardiac, or mobility conditions, seasonal "snowbird" residents, caregivers, and healthcare professionals who refer patients for equipment. The Phoenix metro’s growing 65‑and‑older population and proximity to facilities such as HonorHealth Deer Valley Medical Center and Mayo Clinic Hospital drive demand for post‑discharge and in‑home care equipment.

The company positions itself as a convenient, knowledgeable resource for Phoenix‑area residents and visitors needing reliable home medical equipment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical equipment retail sales", "Medical equipment rental (weekly/monthly)", "Insurance billing assistance (Medicare, major insurers)", "FSA/HSA payment acceptance", "Showroom product demonstration and fitting", "Product consultation for patients, caregivers, and healthcare professionals"], "industries": ["Home healthcare", "Durable medical equipment (DME) retail", "Medical supplies retail", "Senior care", "Respiratory therapy equipment", "Mobility equipment rental"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest medical supply showroom in Arizona", "Fully assembled equipment ready to try before you buy", "Sale or rental options (weekly/monthly)", "Accepts FSA/HSA and works with major insurance providers including Medicare", "Multiple locations across the Phoenix metro area"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Over 22 years in business -> page /", "Largest medical supply showroom in Arizona -> page /", "Sells and rents durable medical equipment (power lift chairs, hospital beds, wheelchairs, scooters, CPAP/BiPAP, oxygen concentrators, etc.) -> page /", "Showroom with fully assembled equipment for trial -> page /", "Accepts FSA/HSA and works with Medicare, Aetna, BCBS AZ, Devoted Health, Homelink, Integrated Home Care Services, One Call, Prospect Medical Group -> page /", "Additional locations in Tempe, Mesa, Surprise -> page /", "Serves patients, caregivers, healthcare professionals, snowbird residents -> page /", "Located near HonorHealth Deer Valley Medical Center and Mayo Clinic Hospital -> page /", "Offers weekly/monthly rentals for mobility equipment -> page /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Copper Star Home Medical has been Phoenix''s locally trusted home medical equipment store for over 22 years.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='copper-star-home-medical-supplies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Copper Wolf Custom Fabrication operates from Golden, Colorado, in the foothills of the Rocky Mountains. After years of running a fabrication shop together, the couple struck out on their own in 2018 to establish CWCF as an independent operation.

The shop focuses on custom metal fabrication, producing handmade furnishings, décor, garden gates, handrails, railings, and stairs.

The company is a member of the Golden Chamber of Commerce, reflecting its local roots.

The Longs emphasize American‑sourced materials, recycled lumber, and a powder‑coat system rated for harsh outdoor exposure as the foundation of their product durability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Welding", "Powder coating", "Custom furniture and decor", "Garden gates", "Handrails and railings", "Metal stairs"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Architectural metalwork"], "materials": ["American grade steel", "Recycled lumber", "Powder coating"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All items made from 100% American-grade steel and recycled lumber", "Durable indoor/outdoor rated powder coating on every piece", "Custom-made to order; no stock inventory", "Family-owned and operated since 2014", "Member of the Golden Chamber of Commerce"], "facts_used": ["Located in Golden, Colorado -> /", "Owned by Chris and Rebecca Long -> /", "Inception year 2014 -> db", "Started independent business in 2018 -> /", "Specializes in custom metal furnishings, decor, gates, handrails, railings, stairs -> /", "Uses 100% American grade steel and recycled lumber -> /", "Powder coated with durable indoor/outdoor rated powder coat -> /", "All items custom-made to order -> /", "Proud member of Golden Chamber of Commerce -> /", "Small business -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Copper Wolf Custom Fabrication is a small Colorado based fabrication shop located in Golden, CO. CWCF specializes in all custom handmade furnishings, decor, garden gates, handrails, as well as many other custom pieces.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='copper-wolf-custom-fabrication' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Corbitt Manufacturing Company operates from Paragould, Arkansas, where it was founded in 1948. The business began as a diversified contract manufacturer specializing in permanent-mold aluminum castings. In 2019, the company was acquired by The Greenbrier Companies and now operates as a Greenbrier subsidiary.

The 100,000-square-foot facility houses three CNC machining centers and three furnaces feeding multiple pour lines. Core capabilities include permanent-mold aluminum castings up to 75 pounds (maximum mold size 48 by 62 inches), CNC machining with wire and RAM EDM, grinding, broaching, and milling, plus captive support services such as fabrication, hot and cold forming, progressive stamping, punching, bending, and welding. The shop handles production runs from single prototypes to several hundred thousand units and offers in-house heat treating, assembly, and reverse engineering.

Corbitt serves OEMs in earth moving, mining, agricultural, electrical, transportation, recreation, food service, construction, industrial tool, farm, and powertrain/transmission sectors. In transportation, it produces dock cleats, transmission casings, manifolds, and railroad car parts. For food service, it re-engineered motor housings for garbage disposals to eliminate leakage. Electrical customers receive explosion-proof receptacles and power line connectors, while powertrain clients rely on the permanent-mold process for gearboxes requiring tight tolerances.

The company emphasizes problem-solving engineering, with a team that brings troubleshooting expertise to every project. Its in-house testing protocols enable fast-tracked deployment of parts to customer fleets, and it promotes competitive pricing across the full volume spectrum.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Permanent-mold aluminum casting", "CNC machining", "Wire EDM", "RAM EDM", "Grinding", "Broaching", "Milling", "Fabrication", "Hot forming", "Cold forming", "Progressive stamping", "Punching", "Bending", "Welding", "Custom tooling", "Jig and fixture manufacturing", "Gear manufacturing", "Assembly", "Heat treating", "Reverse engineering", "Prototype design", "Just-in-time delivery"], "industries": ["Earth moving", "Mining", "Agricultural", "Electrical", "Transportation", "Recreation", "Food service", "Construction", "Industrial tool", "Farm", "Powertrain/Transmission"], "materials": ["Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Dake 375-ton hydraulic press", "Bliss SC2 500-ton press", "Niagara HBM 175-ton press", "Neff CNC custom punch unit", "Esab Shadow 2 burn table", "3 CNC machining centers", "3 furnaces", "SolidWorks"], "volume": "Prototype to several hundred thousand units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Permanent-mold aluminum casting up to 75 lbs (max mold 48\u00d762 in)", "In-house heat treating for shorter cycles and greater process control", "Reverse engineering and prototype design services", "Just-in-time delivery programs", "Captive fabrication, stamping, and welding available as standalone services"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1948 -> db", "Headquarters Paragould, Arkansas -> db", "Acquired by The Greenbrier Companies in 2019 -> /about", "100,000 sq ft facility with 3 CNC machining centers and 3 furnaces -> /about", "Permanent-mold aluminum castings up to 75 lbs, max mold 48x62 in -> /services", "Machining: CNC, wire EDM, RAM EDM, grinding, broaching, milling -> /services", "Support services: fabrication, hot/cold forming, progressive stamping, punching, bending, welding -> /services", "Production volume from prototypes to several hundred thousand units -> /about", "Industries: earth moving, mining, agricultural, electrical, transportation, recreation, food service, construction, industrial tool, farm, powertrain/transmission -> / and /about", "Transportation examples: dock cleats, transmission casings, manifolds, railroad car parts -> /", "Food service example: re-engineered garbage disposal motor housings -> /", "Electrical examples: explosion-proof receptacles, power line connectors -> /", "Powertrain: gearboxes with tight tolerances -> /", "In-house heat treating for shorter cycles -> /services", "Reverse engineering and prototype design -> /services", "Just-in-time delivery -> /services", "Captive support services available standalone -> /services", "Equipment: Dake 375-ton hydraulic press, Bliss SC2 500-ton press, Niagara HBM 175-ton press, Neff CNC custom punch unit, Esab Shadow 2 burn table -> /services", "Software: SolidWorks -> /services", "Company type: contract manufacturer -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1948, Corbitt Manufacturing Company has specialized in diversified contract-manufacturing.", "founded_year": "1948", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='corbitt-manufacturing-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Corporate Casuals operates from Concord, Massachusetts, where it has provided custom embroidery and printing services since 1980. The company runs a production facility in the historic town with a staff of approximately 15 people.

The business decorates a wide range of apparel and accessories—including polo shirts, jackets, fleece, hats, bags, and scrubs—using industrial embroidery machines and printing equipment. A proprietary production system allows on-demand fulfillment of single-unit orders, and the facility has decorated more than 8 million items to date. Customers can upload logos or use an online design studio to create artwork.

Corporate Casuals serves corporate clients, small businesses, and organizations that need branded merchandise for employees, customers, or events. The company stocks premium brands such as The North Face, Nike, Under Armour, Carhartt, and Marmot, and also supplies healthcare-oriented scrubs and lab coats as well as activewear for fitness and outdoor groups.

