UPDATE companies SET description='Cumberland Plastic Solutions operates from Opelika, Alabama, where it was founded in 2006 as a family-owned business. The company began as a custom injection molder and has grown into a full-service contract manufacturer with in-house tooling and automated assembly capabilities.

The facility spans 215,000 square feet of climate-controlled manufacturing and warehouse space and houses 43 precision injection molding machines ranging from 90 to 1,500 tons. A fully equipped tool room handles mold maintenance, engineering changes, and full tool construction from design to production. Value-added secondary operations include sonic and vibration welding, heat staking, leak testing, pad printing, and automated sub-assembly. The quality lab is equipped with a CMM, 3D scanner, optical comparator, and in-house PPAP capabilities.

The company serves the automotive, renewable energy, powersports, lawn and garden, and building and construction industries. In automotive, it supports programs from initial part and tool design through start of series production. For renewable energy, it produces parts that must perform under changing temperature and weather conditions.

Cumberland emphasizes end-to-end contract manufacturing, from product design assistance, material selection, and mold flow analysis to packaging design and final delivery. Its re-sourcing program manages tool transfers to minimize downtime, and a dedicated cross-functional program management team provides weekly progress reports. The IATF 16949:2016 certified quality system underpins continuous improvement across the product lifecycle.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16949:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Two-shot (2K) injection molding", "High-gloss tooling and molding", "In-house tool design and construction", "Mold maintenance and engineering changes", "Sonic/vibration welding", "Heat staking", "Leak testing", "Pad printing", "Automated sub-assembly", "Automated assembly with vision systems", "Poke-yoke error proofing", "Product design assistance", "Tooling design for manufacturability consultation", "Material selection", "Mold flow and warp/shrink analysis", "Packaging design", "Program management for new product development", "Re-sourcing and tool transfer management", "In-house PPAP", "CMM inspection", "3D scanning inspection", "Optical comparator inspection", "ERP and EDI logistics integration"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Renewable Energy", "Powersports", "Lawn & Garden", "Building & Construction"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["43 injection molding machines (90\u20131,500 tons)", "VMC Machining Center", "CMM", "3D scanner", "Optical Comparator"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["215,000 sq ft climate-controlled manufacturing and warehouse space", "43 injection molding machines from 90 to 1,500 tons", "In-house full-service tool room for maintenance, repairs, and new tool builds", "IATF 16949:2016 certified quality system", "Automated assembly with real-time quality monitoring work cells"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2006 -> db", "Family-owned -> /", "Headquarters Opelika, AL -> /capabiliti